  "Validated by _source/state-machines.schema.json before a byte is written. Both generators also refuse: an evidence id docs/spec does not define, a transition whose state keys are not states or whose event is not an event, and a union without exactly one initial state.",
  "HOW A KEY IS READ (decision 4 of CR-436): what is left of a state key after its parent key is either two words (axis.kind -- the axes under one parent are orthogonal and compose) or one word (a kind of the parent's own single union). A key segment {name} in a transition target names a carried value of the event and stands for any kind of that union but its initial one.",
  "Guard expressions and effect bodies are NOT here -- the code holds them (SD-3). Every string that is printed prose is a language dictionary."
